**Technical Specification Document: Extraction and Processing Operations**

**Project Name:** EcoMiner Extraction and Processing Optimization  
**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Prepared by:** GreenTech Solutions, LLC  
**Location:** Silver Creek Mine, Nevada  

**Overview:**  
This document outlines the technical specifications for the extraction and processing of rare earth elements (REEs) at the Silver Creek Mine, including compliance with environmental regulations as set forth by the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) and the Nevada Division of Environmental Protection (NDEP).

**Extraction Requirements:**  
The extraction process will utilize the continuous miner system, Model CM-3000, developed by Advanced Mining Technologies, Inc. The operation is expected to commence on November 1, 2023, with a target output of 1,500 tons of ore per day, employing a workforce of 50 operators trained by SafetyFirst Training Solutions. 

**Processing Details:**  
Ore processing will be conducted using the HydroX Separation System from AquaTech Industries. The system must achieve a minimum recovery rate of 90% for neodymium (Nd) and dysprosium (Dy). A dedicated processing facility will be constructed adjacent to extraction sites, with a completion target date of December 15, 2023. The facility will adhere to ISO 14001 environmental management standards.

**Environmental Compliance:**  
GreenTech Solutions will work closely with the EPA and NDEP to ensure all operations comply with the Clean Water Act and Clean Air Act. Water discharge limits will be established at 100 mg/L for suspended solids, and air quality monitoring will be conducted by AirMonitor Corp. quarterly, starting December 2023.

**Equipment Specifications:**  
All extraction equipment, including the CM-3000, must undergo bi-annual maintenance by TechServ Maintenance Group. The HydroX System will require real-time monitoring systems provided by EnviroTech Sensors, ensuring continuous compliance with environmental metrics.

**Relationships and Dependencies:**  
GreenTech Solutions will coordinate with the local community of Silver Creek, incorporating feedback from the Silver Creek Environmental Committee to address any concerns related to noise and air quality. The project timeline is dependent on timely equipment delivery from Advanced Mining Technologies, with penalties for delays exceeding 10 days post-November 1. 

**Reporting:**  
Progress reports will be generated monthly and reviewed by the project management team, including Project Manager Lisa Tran, Environmental Compliance Officer John Smith, and Operations Supervisor Michael Chen, ensuring that all stakeholders remain informed and engaged throughout the project lifecycle. 

**Conclusion:**  
This technical specification sets forth the critical requirements for successful extraction and processing operations at Silver Creek Mine, balancing operational efficiency with stringent environmental compliance standards.